From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:47:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: the sticks' directions as keys, and a dualsense input
 mode

A keyboard-mode profile binds keys to the sticks' directions as to buttons
(left_stick_up = w, ... right_stick_right = right): each is down while
its stick is pushed that way past the middle of its travel, and up again
once the stick is back inside a little less (pw_wine_stick_buttons), so
W A S D can follow a stick; the stick the pointer follows sends none.
They take bits scePadRead never sets, after the 17 buttons.

mode = dualsense is accepted (PW_GAME_INPUT_DUALSENSE): the game is to
find the DualSense as Windows does a plugged-in one instead of an Xbox
controller.

The catalog test follows the library's size (128 since PC5's first patch).
